BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:black-friday-20261127@todaycelebrates.com
DTSTAMP:20261014T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261127
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261128
SUMMARY:Black Friday
DESCRIPTION:Black Friday is the Friday after Thanksgiving and the conventio
 nal opening of the American Christmas shopping season. The tidy explanatio
 n of its name — that it marks the day retailers' books finally turn from
  red ink to black — is not where the term came from\, and Britannica cal
 ls that version untrue. The phrase began as a complaint about crowds\, in 
 Philadelphia\, and was rebranded into a compliment by retailers roughly a 
 quarter of a century later.\n\nhttps://todaycelebrates.com/holiday/black-f
 riday/
URL;VALUE=URI:https://todaycelebrates.com/holiday/black-friday/
CATEGORIES:Celebration
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CLASS:PUBLIC
SEQUENCE:0
END:VEVENT
