DTSTAMP:20261014T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271011
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271012
SUMMARY:Columbus Day
DESCRIPTION:Columbus Day falls on the second Monday in October and is one o
 f the eleven legal public holidays named in federal law. Its statutory his
 tory is much shorter than its popular one: Americans marked October 12 for
  well over a century before Congress added the day to the federal list in 
 1968 — in the same act that moved it off October 12 and onto a Monday. M
 any states and cities now observe Indigenous Peoples' Day instead.\n\nhttp
 s://todaycelebrates.com/holiday/columbus-day/
URL;VALUE=URI:https://todaycelebrates.com/holiday/columbus-day/
CATEGORIES:Celebration
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CLASS:PUBLIC
SEQUENCE:0
END:VEVENT
