 ober\, the same day as the federal Columbus Day holiday\, and in a great m
 any places it is marked instead of it. It began as a municipal decision: i
 n 1992\, weeks before the 500th anniversary of Columbus's arrival\, Berkel
 ey\, California renamed the day — the first city in the United States to
  do so. It is not itself a federal holiday.\n\nhttps://todaycelebrates.com
 /holiday/indigenous-peoples-day/
URL;VALUE=URI:https://todaycelebrates.com/holiday/indigenous-peoples-day/
CATEGORIES:Celebration
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CLASS:PUBLIC
SEQUENCE:0
END:VEVENT
