UID:labor-day-20270906@todaycelebrates.com
DTSTAMP:20261014T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270906
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270907
SUMMARY:Labor Day
DESCRIPTION:Labor Day falls on the first Monday in September and honors the
  American labor movement and the people whose work built the country. It b
 egan as a union parade in New York City on a Tuesday in September 1882\, s
 pread one state legislature at a time through the 1880s\, and became a fed
 eral holiday in June 1894 — in the middle of a national railroad strike 
 that federal troops had been sent to break. The timing is part of the stor
 y\, not a coincidence.\n\nhttps://todaycelebrates.com/holiday/labor-day/
URL;VALUE=URI:https://todaycelebrates.com/holiday/labor-day/
CATEGORIES:Celebration
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CLASS:PUBLIC
SEQUENCE:0
END:VEVENT
