DTSTAMP:20261014T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261103
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261104
SUMMARY:U.S. General Election Day
DESCRIPTION:U.S. General Election Day falls on the Tuesday after the first 
 Monday in November\, which pins it somewhere between November 2 and Novemb
 er 8. It is the day Americans elect members of Congress and\, every fourth
  year\, the presidential electors who formally choose the president. Three
  separate federal statutes\, passed seventy years apart\, are what put all
  of that on the same Tuesday.\n\nhttps://todaycelebrates.com/holiday/u-s-g
 eneral-election-day/
